text = "# END USER LICENSE AGREEMENT

**Version 26.0, dated August 8, 2026**

This End User License Agreement (the “Agreement”) governs the terms and conditions under which the software product **“Four Nights at Teto”** (the “Title”) may be used, including its software, graphical assets, audiovisual works, textual materials, sound effects, updates, and other components comprising the Title.
The Title is distributed free of charge. No fee is required to obtain a license to use the Title.
By installing, downloading, copying, launching, or otherwise interacting with the Title, the User acknowledges that they have read this Agreement and agree to be bound by its terms.
If the User does not agree to this Agreement, they may discontinue use of the Title and remove it from their device. The Developer will not pursue the User. At least, not under this Agreement.

## 1. DEFINITIONS
1.1. **“Developer”** means the individual or group of individuals responsible for developing, maintaining, and distributing the Title, as well as any other persons lawfully involved in the creation of the Title.
1.2. **“User”** means any individual who has lawfully obtained access to the Title.
1.3. **“Title”** means the software product, including its executable files, assets, levels, characters, models, textures, sound effects, music, dialogue, narrative elements, and other materials provided by the Developer.
1.4. **“Gameplay”** means the actions performed by the User within the Title, including exploring locations, interacting with objects, solving in-game tasks, attempting to survive, and other activities provided for by the Title.
1.5. **“In-Game Object”** means any object, entity, creature, item, image, or other element existing within the Title.
1.6. **“GitHub”** means platform, within the framework of which distribution Title takes place.

## 2. GRANT OF LICENSE

2.1. The Developer grants the User a unlimited, non-exclusive, transferable, and revocable license to use the Title for any purposes.
2.2. The license is provided free of charge and remains effective for as long as the User complies with the provisions of this Agreement.
2.3. The User does not acquire ownership of the Title or any of its individual components. Providing free access to the Title does not constitute a transfer of any exclusive rights to the software, characters, images, audio materials, or other elements of the Title.
2.4. The User may install and run the Title on a device owned or lawfully used by the User, provided that the User complies with this Agreement.

## 3. RESTRICTIONS

3.1. The User shall not:

a) distribute modified or altered copies of the Title without the fork on GitHub, where such distribution infringes upon the rights of the Developer or other rights holders;
b) decompile, disassemble, or otherwise attempt to investigate the internal structure of the Title, except where expressly permitted by applicable law;
c) extract or distribute individual assets of the Title, including models, textures, sounds, music, and other materials, where doing so infringes upon the rights of the respective rights holders;
d) use the Title or any of its components to create materials falsely represented as official materials of the Developer;
e) remove copyright notices, authorship information, or other legal notices contained within the Title;
f) use third-party software for the purpose of interfering with the operation of the Title or obtaining advantages not intended by its mechanics;
g) claim that the strange silhouette at the end of the hallway is merely a lighting issue without conducting a preliminary investigation.
3.2. The user also agrees whit transfer his soul, on a gratuitous and indefinite basis to Developer, without the subsequent possibility of return soul back to the owner.

## 4. CONTENT OF THE TITLE

4.1. The Title is a horror product and may contain scenes, images, sounds, effects, and other elements intended to create fear, tension, anxiety, or discomfort.
4.2. The User is solely responsible for determining whether they are comfortable with such content.
4.3. The Developer does not guarantee the absence of:
a) sudden sounds;
b) abrupt visual effects;
c) unsettling music;
d) creatures that would prefer not to be referred to as “creatures”;
e) situations in which the User becomes convinced that someone is watching them;
f) consequences resulting from the independent decision to “go in there anyway.”
4.4. Certain elements of the Title may be intentionally ambiguous and may not have a definitive explanation within the narrative.
4.5. If, after playing the Title, the User repeatedly checks whether the door to their room is still closed, the Developer does not consider this an official bug report.

## 5. UPDATES AND MODIFICATIONS

5.1. The Developer may release updates, patches, and additions to the Title.
5.2. Updates may include bug fixes, gameplay changes, modifications to visual or audio effects, additions or removals of content, and other changes.
5.3. The Developer does not guarantee that every feature, mechanic, or characteristic of the Title will remain unchanged in subsequent versions.
5.4. If a bug is discovered that allows the User to complete the Title in fourteen seconds, the Developer reserves the right to fix said bug, even if the User considers it to be “the best mechanic in the game.”

## 6. SAVES AND DATA

6.1. The Developer takes reasonable measures to ensure the proper operation of the Title but does not guarantee the absolute preservation of User data or save files.
6.2. The User is solely responsible for backing up their data where such functionality is provided by the Title or the relevant platform.
6.3. The Developer shall not be responsible for loss of progress resulting from hardware failure, third-party software, operating system behavior, actions of third parties, or other circumstances beyond the Developer’s reasonable control.
6.4. Manually deleting the save folder and subsequently requesting restoration of progress shall not be considered a guaranteed method of data recovery.

## 7. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

7.1. The Title is provided **“AS IS”** and **“AS AVAILABLE”**, to the maximum extent permitted by applicable law.
7.2. The Developer does not guarantee that the Title will be completely free of errors, technical issues, or other defects.
7.3. To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the Developer shall not be liable for:
a) loss of gameplay progress;
b) technical issues caused by the User’s hardware;
c) incompatibility of the Title with a particular device configuration;
d) lost sleep resulting from the decision to play “for five more minutes”;
e) the sudden realization that the noises coming from the hallway were part of the gameplay;
f) the urge to check whether the door the User just closed is still closed;
g) any other consequences arising from the use of the Title that could not reasonably have been anticipated by the Developer.
7.4. Nothing in this Agreement shall limit any rights of the User that cannot be limited under applicable law.

## 8. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY

8.1. All intellectual property rights in the Title and its original components belong to the Developer or the respective rights holders, unless expressly stated otherwise within the Title.
8.2. Providing the User with free access to the Title does not constitute a waiver of any intellectual property rights held by the Developer.
8.3. The User may not use characters, narrative elements, visual materials, audio materials, or other components of the Title outside the scope of legally permitted use without the appropriate fork on GitHub.

## 9. TERMINATION OF THE LICENSE

9.1. The license shall terminate automatically in the event of a material breach of this Agreement by the User.
9.2. The User may also terminate the license at any time by removing the Title from their devices and ceasing all use thereof.
9.3. To completely terminate the agreement, the User is obliged contact whit Developer. Message must contain video, where User on sits on knees and prey to Developer, whit termination of the agreement.
9.4. Upon termination of the license, the User shall cease using the Title and delete copies of the Title under their control, unless otherwise permitted by applicable law. 

## 10. FINAL PROVISIONS

10.1. If any provision of this Agreement is determined to be invalid or unenforceable, the remaining provisions shall remain in full force and effect.
10.2. The failure of the Developer to act upon any particular violation of this Agreement shall not constitute a waiver of the Developer’s right to address similar violations in the future.
10.3. This Agreement constitutes the entire agreement between the User and the Developer regarding the use of the Title.
10.4. Section headings are provided for convenience only and shall not be construed as independent provisions of this Agreement.
10.5. By clicking **“I Agree,”** installing, or launching the Title, the User confirms that they have read this Agreement and accept its terms.
10.6. In the event of uncertainty as to whether an object observed by the User was part of the game environment, the User may assume that it was part of the game environment.
10.7. The Developer does not confirm the validity of the preceding provision.

**END OF AGREEMENT**

This does not grant any in-game advantages."

